    <!-- 1. Statement of Commitment -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-sm font-bold text-deep-charcoal flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="font-mono-label text-xs text-electric-blue font-bold px-2.5 py-1 bg-electric-blue/10 rounded-md">01</span>
        <span>Our Commitment</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-gray font-light">
        <strong>Caul Haus Group, Inc.</strong> (&ldquo;CaulHaus&rdquo;) is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people of all abilities. We believe the web should be accessible, usable, and inclusive for everyone, and we continually audit and improve the user experience of our website in compliance with relevant accessibility standards.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-outline-variant/40">

    <!-- 2. Conformance Standards -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-sm font-bold text-deep-charcoal flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="font-mono-label text-xs text-electric-blue font-bold px-2.5 py-1 bg-electric-blue/10 rounded-md">02</span>
        <span>Conformance Standards</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-gray font-light">
        To ensure an accessible experience, CaulHaus adheres to the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA</strong> published by the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C), and aligns with the requirements of <strong>Title III of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
        These guidelines define how to make web content more accessible to individuals with a wide range of visual, auditory, motor, speech, cognitive, and neurological disabilities.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-outline-variant/40">

    <!-- 3. Key Measures Implemented -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-sm font-bold text-deep-charcoal flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="font-mono-label text-xs text-electric-blue font-bold px-2.5 py-1 bg-electric-blue/10 rounded-md">03</span>
        <span>Key Measures Implemented</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-gray font-light">
        We incorporate accessibility into our design system, markup, and engineering practices across <a href="https://caulhaus.com" class="text-electric-blue underline font-medium">caulhaus.com</a>:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-deep-charcoal text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-mono-label">Semantic HTML &amp; Landmarks</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
            We use valid, semantic HTML5 elements including proper landmark roles (<code>&lt;header&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;article&gt;</code>) to allow screen reader users to navigate logically between sections.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-deep-charcoal text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-mono-label">Keyboard Navigation &amp; Skip Links</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
            All interactive navigation links, dropdown menus, and form fields are operable via standard keyboard controls (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space). We provide a direct &ldquo;Skip to main content&rdquo; link at the very top of each page for rapid keyboard navigation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-deep-charcoal text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-mono-label">Color Contrast &amp; Typography</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
            Our architectural palette is tuned to satisfy or exceed the WCAG AA minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for body copy and 3:1 for large display headers. Text size and spacing can be adjusted by user browsers up to 200% without loss of layout integrity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-deep-charcoal text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-mono-label">Form Accessibility &amp; Clear Labels</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
            All inquiry form fields feature explicit, visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> elements with matching <code>id</code> and <code>for</code> attributes, distinct error outlines, and standard ARIA markup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-deep-charcoal text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-mono-label">Text Alternatives &amp; Motion Controls</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-gray font-light text-sm">
            Informational graphics and team images include descriptive <code>alt</code> text. Background visual shaders are marked with decorative roles and do not convey essential operational data.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

